From ee9fc9a40b86df48e3c1f19e15312aa9a5f230a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ole Algoritme <olealgoritme@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 02:32:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] nvk/rm, vulkan/wsi: zero-copy Win32 present through the
 Helios scanout

On Conduit's Helios adapter a Windows guest can show GPU memory on its
display without the compositor: librmclient's Windows transport opens one
of the host's DRM render nodes, imports RM memory there as a GEM object
and names it in a ScanoutFlip, which the host exports as a dma-buf for the
viewer (guest/rmclient crm_scanout_smoke). The Win32 WSI now presents that
way instead of copying every frame through GDI.

vulkan/wsi (Win32):
- wsi_device::win32.scanout_export/scanout_flip: a driver that can show
  device memory sets them. Swapchains then use a new image type,
  WSI_IMAGE_TYPE_WIN32_SCANOUT: linear images in dedicated device-local
  memory, made presentable once when created (scanout_export) and shown
  by scanout_flip on present, after the CPU wait for rendering that the
  software path already does. No window, DC or DIB is involved, so it
  works for a window that is not on a visible desktop.
- No release event yet: a presented image is held until two later
  presents (one on screen, one the display may still be reading), so
  three or more images rotate FIFO-like.
- FIFO is paced at MESA_WSI_SCANOUT_HZ (default 60, 0 = unpaced) with a
  high-resolution waitable timer; Sleep()'s 15.6 ms tick held it at
  32 fps.
- Formats B8G8R8A8 and R8G8B8A8 (UNORM/SRGB) as XRGB8888/XBGR8888, linear.
  If the images cannot be exported the swapchain falls back to GDI.

nvk/rm (Windows):
- nvkmd_rm_win.c: the Windows counterpart of nvkmd_rm_drm.c's export:
  OS_UNIX_EXPORT_OBJECT_TO_FD into a fresh control channel
  (crm_win_open_device 255), DRM_NVIDIA_GEM_IMPORT_NVKMS_MEMORY on host
  render node NVK_HELIOS_DRI (default 0, crm_win_open_device 512 + n,
  opened on first use) through crm_win_ioctl, one GEM handle per memory
  (closed when the memory is freed, the node when the device is
  destroyed), and crm_win_scanout_flip with an increasing seq.
- librmclient's crm_win_* entry points are loaded as optional symbols;
  NVK sets the WSI hooks only when they are there and NVK_HELIOS_WSI is
  not 0. Flip totals are logged when the device is destroyed.

In win11 on an RTX 5090 (Helios KMD 22.22.307.0), vk_scanout_present at
1920x1080 with three images: 60.0 fps for 30 s (1801 flips, 0 failed,
the KMD's NvFlip counter +1801); unpaced, 2784 fps (27841 flips in 10 s,
0 failed).

Still to do: block-linear images with NVIDIA's DRM modifier (NVK renders
a linear swapchain image through a tiled shadow and a copy), a release
event from the host instead of the fixed hold, and vblank pacing.
